id: 37
hanzi: 双手
pinyin: shuāng shǒu
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Noun

meanings_summary:
  en: both hands; two hands
  es: ambas manos; las dos manos

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Noun | Standard | the two hands of a human being | ambas manos; las dos manos del ser humano | 用双手创造生活 (create a life with both hands)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 历经数天冰雪中的徒步跋涉，年轻子路的双手早已被刺骨的严寒冻得红肿开裂、麻木无知。 | Lìjīng shù tiān bīngxuě zhōng de túbù báshè, niánqīng Zǐlù de shuāngshǒu zǎoyǐ bèi cìgǔ de yánhán dòng de hóngzhǒng kāiliè, mámù-wúzhī. | After days of trekking through ice and snow, young Zilu's hands were already red, chapped, and completely numbed by the bitter frost. | Tras días de marcha a pie bajo la nieve, las manos del joven Zilu estaban amoratadas, agrietadas y totalmente entumecidas por el frío glacial.
  #2 | 广大劳动者凭借勤劳朴实的双手，在平凡的岗位上默默耕耘，创造出了令世人瞩目的伟大辉煌。 | Guǎngdà láodòngzhě píngjiè qínláo pǔshí de shuāngshǒu, zài píngfán de gǎngwèi shàng mòmò gēngyún, chuàngzào chū le lìng shìrén zhǔmù de wěidà huīhuáng. | Relying on industrious, honest hands, laborers toiling silently in ordinary posts have created great glories admired across the world. | Con sus manos laboriosas y honestas, los trabajadores que labran en silencio puestos cotidianos han forjado admirables logros para el mundo.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  举起双手 | raise both hands
  用双手创造 | create with both hands
  双手合十 | put palms together in prayer
  握紧双手 | clench both hands
  勤劳的双手 | industrious hands
  伸出双手 | stretch out both hands

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  白手起家 | bái shǒu qǐ jiā | build up from nothing with bare hands; self-made
  手足情深 | shǒu zú qíng shēn | deep brotherly affection like hands and feet
  妙手回春 | miào shǒu huí chūn | magical hands restore spring; heal patients miraculously
  得心应手 | dé xīn yìng shǒu | what the heart wishes the hand can do; highly skilled

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  双 | shuāng | pair; two; double | par; doble; par de | 又 | right hand / again | 又 (one hand) | 又 (second hand beside it) | 4 | 左右结构 | Ideogrammic compound: ancient oracle bone graph of two birds gripped in a hand (隹+又), simplified into two hands (又+又) held side by side, denoting a pair or two. | Two hands (又+又) working harmoniously side by side as a perfect pair. | Dos manos (又+又) colocadas la una junto a la otra actuando en perfecta armonía. | 55 | EE | 雙
  手 | shǒu | hand; person skilled in craft | mano; persona diestra | 手 | hand | 手 (pictograph of human hand with palm and five fingers) | "" | 4 | 单一结构 | Pictographic depiction of a human hand showing wrist, palm, and extended fingers. | An open human hand with fingers capable of grasping, crafting, and creating. | Una mano humana abierta con dedos ágiles listos para sostener, acariciar y construir. | 214 | Q | ""

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: A matched pair (双) of human hands (手) creates your two working hands (双手).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Un par simétrico (双) de manos humanas (手) conforma ambas manos (双手).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: In Chinese civic ethos, relying on one's two hands is the supreme emblem of self-reliance, honest labor, and filial devotion, rejecting unearned privilege.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: High-level 1st tone followed by dipping 3rd tone: shuāng shǒu (55-214). 'shuāng' sustains clear high pitch before 'shǒu' dips deeply.

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[4]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
    难 | nán | difficult | Has 隹 on the right of 又
    汉 | hàn | Han; Chinese | Has 氵 (water) on the left of 又
    毛 | máo | hair; fur | Curve hooks to the right at bottom, whereas 手 hooks to the left
    才 | cái | talent; only then | Lacks the upper curved slash 丿 of 手
  etymological_cognates[4]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
    双方 | shuāng fāng | both parties; bilateral
    双重 | shuāng chóng | double; dual
    手指 | shǒu zhǐ | finger
    手段 | shǒu duàn | means; method; measure

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 双手 refers specifically to the matched pair of human hands as organs of touch, labor, holding, and care.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 双手 vs. 手 | shǒu | 手 can be singular or generic, whereas 双手 specifically highlights the bilateral pair working in coordination.
    2 | 双手 vs. 手足 | shǒuzú | 双手 denotes anatomical hands, while 手足 literally means hands and feet and metaphorically denotes brothers or close kin.
    3 | 双手 vs. 臂膀 | bìbǎng | 双手 refers strictly to palms and fingers, whereas 臂膀 denotes arms and shoulders, symbolizing strong physical backing.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 虽然风雪交加、滴水成冰，子路的一双手冻得通红麻木，但他依然用双手死死扣住背上的绳索，生怕米袋在剧烈颠簸中滑落，这份深情让天地亦为之动容。 | Suīrán fēngxuě-jiāojiā, dīshuǐ-chéngbīng, Zǐlù de yì shuāngshǒu dòng de tōnghóng mámù, dàn tā yīrán yòng shuāngshǒu sǐsǐ kòuzhù bèishàng de shéngsuǒ, shēngpà mǐdài zài jùliè diānbǒ zhōng huáluò, zhè fèn shēnqíng ràng tiāndì yì wéi zhī dòngróng. | Though wind and snow froze all to ice, and both hands were crimson and numb, Zilu gripped the cords with both hands lest the sack slip on the rough trail, moving heaven and earth. | Pese al temporal gélido y a tener las manos rojas e insensibles, Zilu aferró las cuerdas con ambas manos temiendo que el saco resbalara, conmoviendo al cielo con su lealtad filial.
  #2 | 人类进化的重要里程碑在于直立行走解放了双手。从早期制造简陋的石器打猎割草，到现代操作精密仪器探索深空，人类正是依靠这一双灵巧勤劳的双手，将心中的构想化为现实，创造出灿烂辉煌的物质与精神文明。 | Rénlèi jìnhuà de zhòngyào lǐchéngbēi zàiyú zhílì xíngzǒu jiěfàng le shuāngshǒu. Cóng zǎoqī zhìzào jiǎnlòu de shíqì dǎliè gēcǎo, dào xiàndài cāozuò jīngmì yíqì tànsuǒ shēnkōng, rénlèi zhèng shì yīkào zhè yì shuāng língqiǎo qínláo de shuāngshǒu, jiāng xīnzhōng de gòuxiǎng huàwéi xiànshí, chuàngzào chū cànlàn huīhuáng de wùzhì yǔ jīngshén wénmíng. | A major milestone in human evolution was bipedalism liberating both hands. From crafting stone tools to operating delicate instruments in space, humanity has relied on industrious hands to turn ideals into reality, creating civilization. | El gran hito evolutivo fue la marcha bípeda que liberó ambas manos. Desde las rudimentarias herramientas de piedra hasta los instrumentos espaciales, la humanidad ha transformado sus sueños en realidad gracias a sus manos laboriosas.
